.TH HELP-PAGER 7
.SH NAME
help-pager - browse DiftrayWM manual pages
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Help Pager displays DiftrayWM manual pages inside the focused NCursor cell.
It accepts Unix manpage source and keeps the page open until it is closed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
:help [page]
Open help-index, or the named page.
.TP
:h [page]
Short form of :help.
.TP
:help find {pattern}
Search the current page using an Oniguruma UTF-8 regular expression.
.TP
:help bookmark-set {name}
Bookmark the current page for this compositor session.
.TP
:help bookmark-open {name}
Open a saved bookmark.
.SH NAVIGATION
.TP
/
Open an in-page search prompt. Enter runs the search and Escape cancels it.
.TP
n and ?
Jump to the next and previous matching line after a search.
.TP
Space and b
Move one page down and up. j and k, or the arrow keys, move one line.
.TP
q or Escape
Close the pager.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The general configuration section accepts help_key_close, help_key_search,
help_key_next, help_key_previous, help_key_page_down, help_key_page_up,
help_key_line_down, and help_key_line_up. Values are literal one-character
keys, or space, PageDown, PageUp, Up, and Down.
.SH FILES
help_path names a colon-separated set of directories containing page.1 files.
